Read `IDH-ticket-briefs.md`, `REPORT.md`, `controls.json` and `reproduce.py`;
all four and `scripts/compare_assess.py` byte-match the handoff commit.

Receiving checks (2026-11-26, IDH base
`44c0e4f1619689a87786418b77ba7b6d93bf18f6`):

1. Facts versus framing: reran `raw_boundary_without_run`, a disjoint complete
   16-criterion partition. With no reproduction rows, no execution coverage,
   `paper` blocked and an unresolved raw/analysis boundary, `derive_table`
   emits `repro_raw=Partially`. Independent positive control: complete raw
   coverage plus an actual matching `crr:x` comparison emits Fully. The empty
   run is therefore not a broken-reader inference.
2. Duplicates/overlap: no open duplicate or PR implementation found. Closed
   1562 explicitly introduced the examined-boundary Partially interpretation;
   closed 1563 separately says blocked/execution evidence remains unassessed.
   This is a new demonstrated scientific consequence of that exception, not
   a claim those earlier changes never landed. Related 1565 concerns provision
   completeness, not numerical execution.
3. Ownership: IDH owns the assessment contract; replicator owns its boundary
   override/comparator and the trial. An implementation there requires its
   own receiving pickup and validation.
4. Standing rulings/current fit: prior 1562 requested a stated reading for an
   undecidable split and accepted Partially; that history is explicit. This
   receiving report challenges applying that provision judgment to numerical
   execution. No contrary author ruling found mandating a numerical partial
   result without execution. Accept the defect for Imagine, with any changed
   target interpretation declared before validation; filing authorizes no
   implementation or expansion of objectives.

## Observation and scientific impact

`skills/replicate/references/assessment.md:151-160` explicitly allows the
ambiguous raw/analysis boundary to make the from-raw execution row Partially,
and the table at line 187 repeats it. Lines 189-200 otherwise require
execution/output-inventory evidence and keep unexamined comparisons unassessed.
Replicator `scripts/compare_assess.py:204-216` applies the boundary override
last, after resetting blocked execution to unassessed. Thus this is specified
behavior with conflicting semantics, not a parser accident.

The unchanged frozen Blair dossier also takes this exception without a run.
That does not prove the unseen raw boundary or correct I4R label; the verified
fact is the no-run categorical result. A numerical reproducibility category
currently carries a provision/boundary judgment instead of output comparisons.

## Bounded requested outcome

Retain raw/analysis boundary uncertainty in its own evidence field and keep
numerical execution unassessed until execution evidence exists. A verified
analysis-only package may still justify an explicitly labelled provision-based
impossibility/No; distinguish that basis from an observed failed run. Do not
force agreement with I4R by changing frozen observations or comparison scope.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] An unresolved raw/analysis boundary without execution comparisons cannot
      generate numerical execution Partially; uncertainty remains explicit.
- [ ] Actual partial matches can still generate Partially under the declared
      execution-coverage rules; a complete-match positive control still yields
      Fully, and verified impossibility is distinguished from observed failure.
- [ ] Assessment/report instructions and the six-row derivation distinguish
      inspection from execution consistently. Validate the boundary-without-run,
      observed-partial and complete-match controls and unchanged frozen Blair
      dossier before any new cohort; preserve prior observations.

## Verification limits and scope

Receiver verified the four supplied full-grid controls, the independent
complete-match execution positive control and 50 frozen deliverable hashes
and sizes. No scientific package was run and no source/dossier was written.
No skill rewrite or replicator comparator edit is included in this filing.
Adapter tolerance, matched output scope and future trial design are protocol
questions, not extra accepted defects. Tracker 1552 remains open.
